      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is intentional.  I have some more to learn about how vboot works before I try to preserve information across a sysjump.  I want to get the least-complex diagnostic out there first.  That way it doesn\u0027t take too much work to interpret the logs when using them to debug the AP.\n\nIt also doesn\u0027t help that I just spent most of a week debugging an issue that was (partially) caused by an incomplete save/restore of state through bbsram :)\n\nGrunt also experiences a double-start when powered up for the first time, once on initial power-on, and once more by the H1.  The result is that some interesting startup conditions are only visible on the EC console; they are not visible using the UPTIME_INFO command since the condition has cleared by the time of the second EC start.",
      "parentUuid": "520d2787_1bcb32bf",
